#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Island, the maintainer's own first play (#126), from its boot through
# the Information Center and up its observation deck, then out of its door and
# away on the bicycle to the beach, where the window was closed.
#
# Played by hand at a window on the maintainer's MacBook, with --audio and
# --record, on b90b1d7 (lego-island 0.1.0, core 1.1.0), and signed off on
# 2026-10-21: "It works. Hooray!" Recorded, not written; nothing below is
# edited but these comments.
#
# A click at flip 653 skips the intro, and one at 1071 the Infomaniac's
# welcome. The book on the desk opens at 1265; O, O and the tick sign it as
# OO, and the players, Players.gsi, are written at flip 1678. Right of the
# main room is the score room, then the room with the revolving door and the
# elevator, whose top button rides up to the observation deck at about 3300.
# There its controls turn the sky pink, orange, dark and back to a light
# orange, and a paper plane flies, until 4373; the elevator comes down, and
# the rooms are gone round again, the score room's history book opened at
# about 6300. Back in the main room, Pepper's portrait, the third, is picked at
# 7538 and framed in blue, and films play in the map's frame until about
# 8700. Right, right, and the revolving door at 9142: outside from about 9300.
# Up walks to the red bicycle, a click at 9547 gets on it, and Up, steered
# with Left and Right, rides it from 9645 to 10287, under the sky the deck
# left light orange, down to the beach. It looks out over the sea from there
# until the window is closed at flip 10667, instruction 3,341,815,783.
#
# A route keeps what a person did, not the window closing, so it ends at its
# last move, at flip 10626; the replay is held to the instruction the play
# was stopped at by its budget. The play began from an empty profile, its
# log finding no players and no scores at boot, and every replay starts from
# an empty data root too, so that changes nothing. Closing the window does not
# tell the game, so the players are all it saved; the game and the scores are
# written at the quit door or as the game closes itself (#140).
